{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>And as for the people, he moved them.</b> Yosef from city to city, as a reminder that they no longer have a share in the land — and he settled the people of this city in its fellow, and Scripture had no need to write this except to inform you of Yosef's merit, that he intended to remove shame from his brothers, so they would not be called exiles (Ḥullin 60a)." "<b>From one end of the border of Egypt, etc.</b> So he did to all the cities that are in the kingdom of Egypt, from one end of its border to the end of its border."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 47, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:03:49.789126293Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}